ok - an unset seat setting is the ambient default and configures no automatic switching
ok - a switch to a logged-in seat records the seat and nothing else
ok - a switch to a profile that is not logged in is refused and changes nothing
ok - --force does not override a seat proven to be logged out
ok - a rate-limited signed-in seat is undecided, and --force switches onto it
ok - an unreadable credential store reads as undecided and --force may cross it
ok - a forced switch refuses a seat whose profile directory does not exist
ok - switching to the default seat clears the setting and restores ambient behaviour
ok - a seat switch reaches running local secondmate homes and reports each one
ok - a failed secondmate push is reported and never undoes the primary switch
ok - a local home that declines keeps its own three seat settings through a switch
ok - one home's decline leaves every other local home taking the switch
ok - status names every local home that declined and the seat it is really on
ok - a decline flag of any type declines and shows in status
ok - seat settings reach local secondmate homes only and never cross to a remote route
ok - a seat switch pushes only local secondmate homes and never waits on a remote route
ok - fm-config-push reaches remote routes by default and skips them only with --local-only
ok - the auto-switch threshold is configurable, validated, clearable, and unset by default
ok - the threshold condition turns true exactly at the configured percent
ok - an unreadable quota never trips an automatic switch
ok - only account-level quota windows count toward the auto-switch threshold
ok - the default seat's probe and threshold read the ambient profile new workers launch with
ok - a home that configures none of the automatic settings behaves exactly as before they existed
ok - the dispatch gate reads no quota at all until an extra-usage policy is configured
ok - the destination minimum is settable by command, validated, clearable, and unset by default
ok - a switch skips a logged-in seat below the destination minimum and lands on one above it
ok - no switch happens when every candidate is below the destination minimum
ok - a candidate whose quota gives no verdict is skipped, never guessed at as headroom
ok - the extra-usage policy is settable by command, validated, clearable, and unset by default
ok - the stop policy holds new dispatch only once the active seat's plan quota is gone
ok - the allow policy dispatches under its dollar cap and holds once the spend reaches it
ok - an unreadable quota holds dispatch instead of guessing, and the hold lifts once it reads again
ok - the watch keeps running after a switch, fires once per crossing, and catches the next seat's own
ok - with no seat qualifying the watch reports the policy consequence once and switches nothing
ok - the watch's wake line and status agree while the seat still has plan quota
ok - after a crossing with nowhere to go, the watch keeps looking and switches once a seat recovers
ok - every quota read one automatic pass makes stays inside the watcher's per-check budget
ok - the watch switches nothing when the active seat's quota gives no verdict
ok - arm registers a repeating watch the watcher can run, and retire removes it cleanly
ok - status reports all three automatic settings, every percentage counting percent left
ok - rotation chooses the next logged-in seat under the root and skips ones with no credentials
ok - rotation never targets the default profile, even when it is the only other logged-in store
ok - rotation never assumes which seats exist and picks up seats added later
ok - rotation refuses rather than pretending to switch when no other seat is usable
ok - adding a seat creates an empty profile directory and prints the owner's login steps
ok - a directory named 'default' is never offered, added, or rotated to
ok - seat names that are not a single safe path component are refused
ok - an unset seat setting leaves the launch and the task record exactly as before
ok - a spawn launches on the active seat and records it in the task's own record
ok - switching seats leaves a running worker's recorded profile unchanged
ok - after a switch new workers get the new seat while existing ones keep theirs
ok - an ambient CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR still reaches workers and is recorded per task
ok - a configured seat takes precedence over firstmate's own ambient config dir
ok - a non-claude spawn records no Claude seat while a named seat is active
ok - a home configuring both an account pin and an active seat is refused before anything exists
ok - an account pin refuses relaunching a task recorded on a seat before anything is touched
ok - a pin-only home with no seat file still relaunches a claude task under its pin
ok - a pin pointing at a seat directory still relaunches a task recorded on that directory
ok - a stop policy holds a fresh claude spawn, names the override, and changes nothing when overridden
ok - the spawn gate holds at the dollar cap and on an unreadable quota, and dispatches under the cap
ok - the dispatch hold covers fresh claude spawns only and never strands a task already under way
ok - the Claude extra-usage hold never reaches a worker on another harness
# all fm-seat tests passed
